  "status_statement": "Mapping of the 61 product acceptance criteria in spec 1.2.0 to planned evaluation suites and named audits. Nothing here is evidence of product capability and no criterion is marked validated. Five criteria have a built evaluator slice (C-02-AC1, C-02-AC2, C-02-AC3, C-09-AC1, C-09-AC3); the C-02-AC3 slice also restores a pre-deletion backup, and all built slices remain small, synthetic and deterministic. The two capabilities added in 1.2.0 (C-13, C-14) have no fixture and no slice.",
  "status_vocabulary": {
    "planned_suite": "an evaluation family or task type is named; no task set exists yet",
    "named_audit": "measurement is an audit, inventory review or egress probe rather than a task outcome",
    "human_review": "requires human judgement; no automatable proxy has been identified",
    "blocked_owner_input": "the suite can be prepared but cannot produce a valid result without the named owner input or G-O1",
    "slice_built": "an implemented evaluator slice exercises part of this criterion and its gates run on synthetic fixtures; still not product validation, and the slice may cover only part of the metric"
  },
